  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BRCiS IRF 2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To avert negative coping strategies, morbidity, and mortality, BRCiS will scale up the humanitarian response to the ongoing drought in Somalia through the provision of Multipurpose Cash Assistance (MPCA) and community water vouchers. This will ensure that vulnerable households are able to meet their basic needs and withstand the impacts of the drought.The project will target marginalised communities in districts that are most affected by the drought, identified through the established BRCiS Early Warning Early Action system and recent drought assessments. This ensures that support can be targeted to the most vulnerable, with particular consideration of households that are least likely to withstand the impact of the drought without external assistance. The primary objective is to support vulnerable populations to cope with the current drought, reducing their likelihood of displacement, which has a significantly higher risk of mortality</narrative>
  </description>
